! mcp_bootstrap_p221.strap -- MCP printed page 221: the Input Program's
! tape write/read section (V WF1 .. V RTEE), lines 1-48.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.228, read at 400 dpi, 900/1800 dpi
! for doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11D11MCP  CARD ID CA000335  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 221";
! the heading row's LOCATION field is 224377, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  48 lines, every one located, contiguous from 224377.00 to
! 224427.40 (a half word; next word 224430.00).  The volume OCR puts
! printed p.220's last row at 224376.40 (remark -0344) and p.222's first
! at 224430.00 (remark -0389), so the page joins on both sides; this
! page's remarks run -0345 .. -0388 (octal sequence numbers, e.g.
! -0357 then -0360), and some rows print none.
!
! >>> THE V SYMBOLS ARE PRINTED p.213'S, WHICH IS NOT LANDED. <<<  p.213
! ("THE INPUT PROGRAM") prints the SYN table: V F SYN,.32; V H SYN,32;
! V M1 SYN(BU,64),262143.; V X2S = 1.0; V CWR = 4.0; V SU = 6.0;
! V RCNT = 7.0; V FCNX = (8)11.0; V U $3, V P $1, V T3 $7, V T4 $8,
! V T5 $9.  Read off p.213's image (PDF p.220) and every one agrees with
! this page's binary.  The rest (V WT, V WTTS, V MD, V WCW, V PD, V TSQ,
! V TEE, V QEND, V Q, V TEE1, V RT, V RQ1, V ST) come from this page's
! binary only, as noted per card.
!
! LINES 29 AND 32, "V+ICR,V T3,.V H" -> 000000.57 07: ".V H" is a bit
! part of V H = 32 bits, i.e. 0.40, and .40 + .17 (2*7+1) = .57.  A
! bit address is "a pair of integers separated by a period" and an
! integer may be "a symbol that takes on an integral value" (C22-6531
! printed p.10); p.213 prints V H as the integer 32 (+00000040).  These
! two rows failed until the assembler read a symbol after the period.
!
! >>> "V WIC" IS WRITTEN VWIO. <<<  Line 10's last glyph at 1800 dpi has
! the straight sides and squared corners of the O in V RTIO (line 37)
! and V WTEOP (line 7), broken on the right with stroke remnants, not
! the round C beside it in SIC.  It pairs with V RTIO.  Nothing on this
! page references it (a later page's "B,V WIC" OCR prints 224403.50,
! the address, not the spelling) -- rests on ink.
!
! Octal-field opens ("C00007.CC", "224707.5C") are 0.  Hex bytes printed
! with an open round, written 0: line 3 "C0" and lines 11/36 "C0" (B,
! with no index is 00, as lines 12/39/45 print it), line 29 "C7" (= line
! 27/32's 07), line 38 "BC" (M+1(BU,18),V RCNT(V U) has no offset index;
! p.197 line 8 prints the same second half word "022000.22 B0").
!
! >>> CARD SERIALS. <<<  Right-hand serials run ?A000335 .. ?A000376 --
! the prefix glyph has a straight left stem (the D of "ID" beside the
! header's CA000335 is the same shape), so DA by the C/D rule; recorded
! as read either way.  Six pairs share a serial: lines 3/4 (337), 10/11
! (343), 12/13 (344), 22/23 (353), 39/40 (369), 47/48 (376) -- a call
! B,D MCP plus its parameter half word, or SIC plus the branch, two
! statements per card.  Asterisks after the LOCATION on lines 20, 42.

VF      SYN, .32                     ! p.213 line  6 "V F SYN,.32" (not landed); V+ICR line 27 .57
VH      SYN, 32                      ! p.213 line  7 "V H SYN,32" (not landed); .VH line 29 .57
VM1     SYN(BU,64), 262143.          ! p.213 line  9 (not landed); CB- line 6 777777.03
VX2S    SYN, 1.0                     ! p.213 line 13 = VX1.VH = 1.0 (not landed); LX line 26
VCWR    SYN, 4.0                     ! p.213 line 15 = VX2R+2. = 4.0 (not landed); line 42 000004.00
VSU     SYN, 6.0                     ! p.213 line 18 = VIC.VH = 6.0 (not landed); LVE line 5
VRCNT   SYN, 7.0                     ! p.213 line 20 = VRQB.VH = 7.0 (not landed); SV line 2
VFCNX   SYN, 9.0                     ! p.213 line 24 = VTS.VH = (8)11.0 (not landed); LC line 18
